#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""phone: AgentLab's phone line (after-hours call agent). Read/change its setup and read call logs.

  phone status                       number, worker health, current setup in plain words
  phone config                       full setup as JSON
  phone set '<json>'                 merge a JSON patch into the setup (validated), e.g. phone set '{"greeting":"..."}'
  phone set-followups '<json list>'  replace the after-call follow-up list (plain-language instructions)
  phone calls [-n 10] [--open]       recent calls: time, caller, name, status, message, summary
  phone call <call_id>               one call in full (details + transcript)
  phone handled <call_id> --note "…" mark a call handled (what you did)

Owner controls (all validated; the next call uses them):
  phone on | phone off               turn the phone agent on/off (off: calls are dropped by the AI; set it back on any time)
  phone emergency transfer|text|message    urgent calls: warm-transfer to the targets | text the owner right away | no urgent handling, take a message for the next business day
  phone booking live | request | off | link <https://booking-url>    live = book on the connected calendar; request = just collect the preferred time; link = text the owner's booking link
  phone info '<short facts about the business>'     goes straight into the agent's prompt (hours, address, services, policies)
  phone faq add "Question" "Answer" | phone faq rm "Question" | phone faq list       short Q&A, in the prompt
  phone kb add "Title" --file /path/doc.txt   (or --text '...')   long documents (catalogs, manuals, price lists): searched during calls, not in the prompt
  phone kb list | phone kb rm "Title" | phone kb search "words"
  phone voices | phone voice <name>   list / change the GPT Live voice (next call)
Temporary or scheduled changes (code applies them at call time and they expire by themselves; nothing to restore):
  phone override add '<config patch json>' [--from WHEN] [--until WHEN] [--note "why"]     WHEN = now | tomorrow | monday..sunday | next-open | YYYY-MM-DD | 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM' (business timezone)
      e.g. no transfers tonight:      phone override add '{"emergency":{"policy":"message"}}' --until next-open --note "movies"
           messages not bookings:     phone override add '{"options":{"appointments":"request"}}' --until monday
           Calendly link from tomorrow: phone override add '{"options":{"appointments":"link"},"booking":{"booking_link":"https://calendly.com/x"}}' --from tomorrow
           vacation:                  phone override add '{"greeting":"...","options":{"appointments":"off"}}' --until 2026-12-07
  phone override list | phone override rm <id>
Per caller type (existing = number found in call history or in customers; new = everyone else):
  phone rule existing|new emergency transfer|text|message      phone rule existing|new booking live|request|link|off      phone rule clear existing|new
  phone customers add +1703... | rm +1703... | list
After-call standing instructions (run by the follow-up run after EVERY call):  phone followup add "plain words" | rm <n> | list     Local contacts (CRM fallback): phone contact add "Name" --phone +1.. --email .. --note ".." --call <id> | list | search <text>
phone timing [<call_id>]   per-turn latency table (caller end-of-speech -> GPT Live first audio, tool, Luna steps)    phone cost [-n 10]   per-call cost
First-time setup: phone setup   (checklist of what is still needed)   phone setup done
Self-improvement (owner opt-in; nothing runs by itself, nothing changes without the owner approving):
  phone review [--days 30]           quality evidence from real calls: unanswered questions, abandoned calls, failed bookings, unneeded transfers, wrong captures, top requests
  phone briefing [--day YYYY-MM-DD]  outcomes summary computed from the logs;  phone briefing enable --at 08:00 | disable
  phone watch enable|disable | add <url> [--every DAYS] | rm <url> | list | check [--force] [--quiet]    cheap fetch+diff of the owner's site, only when enabled
  phone proposal add <faq_add|faq_rm|info_set|instructions_add|greeting_set|kb_add> "<question|title>" --text "..." --why "evidence"
  phone proposal list [--all] | show <id> | approve <id> | reject <id>      approve applies it and records it in config history (phone undo reverts)
Change history:  phone history   (what changed, when, diff)     phone undo   (put back the previous setup)
  phone standard <name|callback_number|email|reason> on|off [required|optional] [--ask "wording"]
  phone field add '{"key":"budget","label":"Budget","ask":"What budget do you have in mind?","required":false,"intents":[]}'
  phone field rm <key>            phone field list
  phone intent add '{"name":"new customer","description":"...","fields":["budget"],"questions":["..."],"urgent":false}'
  phone intent rm <name>
  phone closure add '{"date":"2026-12-25","name":"Christmas","message":"..."}'   (or start/end, optional "hours":["10:00","14:00"])
  phone closure rm <date-or-name>
  phone target add '{"name":"Rick","number":"+17038166017"}'   (ordered fallback list: first added rings first)
  phone target rm <number>        phone target clear
Booking setup (times are always in the business timezone; it is required, IANA like America/New_York):
  phone set '{"timezone":"America/New_York"}'
  phone set '{"booking":{"appointment_minutes":30,"buffer_minutes":10,"min_notice_hours":4,"days_ahead":30}}'    (slot length 15|30|60)
  phone set '{"booking":{"booking_hours":{"mon":["09:00","17:00"],"tue":["09:00","17:00"],"wed":null,"thu":["10:00","16:00"],"fri":null,"sat":null,"sun":null}}}'   (give all 7 days; null = no bookings)
  phone holiday list | open <key> | close <key>      US holidays: closed = not bookable (default all closed)
  phone blackout add <YYYY-MM-DD | YYYY-MM-DD..YYYY-MM-DD> [name]   one-off days off   |   phone blackout rm <date> | list
Transfer ring time per number: phone set '{"transfer":{"ring_seconds":30}}'. Hold music: phone set '{"hold_music":{"enabled":true,"path":"/workspace/runs/phone/hold.ogg","volume":0.35}}'.
Modes: phone set '{"mode":"overflow"}' (answer calls forwarded on busy/no-answer), "after_hours", or "always".
Spam: phone set '{"spam":{"enabled":true}}'. Owner alerts: phone set '{"notify":{"when":"every_call|messages|urgent|off","email":true,"sms":true}}'.
"""
import argparse, json, os, sys
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo
sys.path.insert(0, '/opt/tools/pylib_phone'); sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), 'pylib_phone'))
import store  # noqa

TZ = ZoneInfo('America/New_York')


def local(s):
    try:
        return datetime.strptime(s, '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ').replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc).astimezone(TZ).strftime('%a %b %d %I:%M %p ET')
    except Exception:
        return s


def local_iso(s):
    if not s:
        return '-'
    try:
        return datetime.fromisoformat(s).astimezone(TZ).strftime('%a %b %d %I:%M %p ET')
    except Exception:
        return s


def fmt_phone(n):
    """Ready-to-quote US number, e.g. '(571) 477-6175'. Leave other values unchanged."""
    if n is None or n == '':
        return n if n is not None else ''
    digits = ''.join(c for c in str(n) if c.isdigit())
    if len(digits) == 11 and digits.startswith('1'):
        digits = digits[1:]
    if len(digits) == 10:
        return f'({digits[:3]}) {digits[3:6]}-{digits[6:]}'
    return str(n)


def status():
    cfg = store.load_config()
    hb = {}
    try:
        hb = json.load(open(os.path.join(store.PHONE_DIR, 'worker-heartbeat.json')))
    except Exception:
        pass
    age = None
    if hb.get('at'):
        age = (datetime.now(timezone.utc) - datetime.strptime(hb['at'], '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ').replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)).total_seconds()
    base_cfg = cfg
    cfg, _act = store.effective_config(base_cfg)
    for o in base_cfg.get('overrides') or []:
        print(f"Override {o['id']} [{'ACTIVE NOW' if o in _act else 'not active'}]: {json.dumps(o['set'])} from {local_iso(o.get('from'))} until {local_iso(o.get('until'))} {o.get('note') or ''}")
    cr = base_cfg.get('caller_rules') or {}
    if cr.get('existing') or cr.get('new'):
        print(f"Caller-type rules: existing={json.dumps(cr.get('existing'))} new={json.dumps(cr.get('new'))}; extra customers: {len(base_cfg.get('customers') or [])}")
    t = cfg['transfer']
    print(f"Number: {cfg['phone_number']}  enabled={cfg['enabled']}  worker={'UP' if age is not None and age < 120 else 'DOWN?'} (heartbeat {int(age) if age is not None else '?'}s ago)")
    print(f"Mode: {cfg['mode']} (AI answers {'every call' if cfg['mode']=='always' else 'outside business hours'}); business hours now: {store.is_business_hours(cfg)}; tz {cfg['timezone']}")
    print(f"Hours: {json.dumps(cfg['business_hours'])}")
    print(f"During business hours: {cfg['during_business_hours']}")
    print(f"Assistant: {cfg['assistant_name']} voice={cfg['voice']}  Greeting: {cfg['greeting']}")
    print(f"Business info: {cfg['business_info']}")
    o, b, sms = cfg['options'], cfg['booking'], cfg['sms']
    print(f"Options: take messages={o['take_message']}  booking mode={o['appointments']} (live|request|link|off)  transfer={o['transfer']}")
    print(f"Emergency policy: {cfg['emergency']['policy']} (transfer | text the owner | message only for the next business day)")
    print(f"Business info: {len(cfg['business_info'])} chars in prompt; FAQ items: {len(cfg.get('faq') or [])}; knowledge base docs: {len(store.kb_list())}")
    tg = ', '.join(f"{x.get('name')} {fmt_phone(x['number'])}" for x in t.get('targets') or []) or '(none set!)'
    if o.get('transfer'):
        print(f"Transfer: ON {t['mode']} -> {tg}; rings {t['ring_seconds']}s each; when: {t['when']}")
    else:
        print(f"Transfer: off (targets: {tg})")
    hm = cfg['hold_music']
    print(f"Hold music: {'on' if hm['enabled'] else 'off'} {hm['path']} vol {hm['volume']}")
    it = cfg['intake']
    print('Intake (what the agent asks): ' + '; '.join(f"{k}={'ON' if v['on'] else 'off'}{'*' if v['on'] and v['required'] else ''}" for k, v in it['standard'].items()) + '   (* required)')
    for c in it['custom']:
        print(f"  custom {c['key']} [{'required' if c.get('required') else 'optional'}] ask: {c['ask']}" + (f"  only for: {c['intents']}" if c.get('intents') else ''))
    for i in it['intents']:
        print(f"  intent {i['name']}: {i.get('description') or ''} fields={i.get('fields')} questions={i.get('questions')}{' URGENT' if i.get('urgent') else ''}")
    for c in cfg.get('closures') or []:
        print(f"  closure {c.get('date') or (c['start'] + '..' + c['end'])} {c.get('name') or ''} {c.get('hours') or 'closed'}")
    nt = cfg['notify']
    print(f"Owner alerts: when={nt['when']} email={nt['email']} -> {nt['owner_email']}  sms={nt['sms']} -> {[fmt_phone(n) for n in nt['owner_sms']]}  spam filter={cfg['spam']['enabled']}")
    print(f"Booking: {b['provider']} calendar={b['calendar_id'] or 'default'} tz={cfg['timezone']} {b['appointment_minutes']}min slots, buffer {b['buffer_minutes']}min, next {b['days_ahead']} days, "
          f"min notice {b['min_notice_hours']}h, hold {b['slot_hold_minutes']}min, link={b['booking_link'] or '-'}")
    print(f"  booking hours: {json.dumps(b['booking_hours'] or cfg['business_hours'])}{' (= business hours)' if not b['booking_hours'] else ''}")
    print(f"  closed US holidays: {', '.join(b['holidays']['closed']) or 'none'}; blackout dates: {json.dumps(b['blackout_dates']) if b['blackout_dates'] else 'none'}")
    print(f"SMS: {'on' if sms['enabled'] else 'off'} from {sms['from']} (platform toll-free; a local number needs A2P)  "
          f"confirm-by-text={sms['text_caller_confirmation']} text-link={sms['text_booking_link']}")
    print(f"After call: run agent={cfg['after_call']['run_agent']}; instructions: {cfg['after_call']['instructions']}")
    for i, f in enumerate(cfg['after_call'].get('follow_ups') or [], 1):
        print(f"  follow-up {i}: {f}")
    if cfg.get('extra_instructions'):
        print(f"Extra instructions: {cfg['extra_instructions']}")


def apply(patch):
    cfg = store.load_config()
    new = store._merge(cfg, patch)
    errs = store.validate(new)
    if errs:
        sys.exit('Not saved: ' + '; '.join(errs))
    store.save_config(new)
    print('Saved. The next call uses it.')
    status()


def main():
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog='phone', description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    p.add_argument('cmd', nargs='?', default='status')
    p.add_argument('arg', nargs='?')
    p.add_argument('arg2', nargs='?')
    p.add_argument('arg3', nargs='?')
    p.add_argument('--ask', default=None)
    p.add_argument('--from', dest='frm', default=None)
    p.add_argument('--until', default=None)
    p.add_argument('--file', default=None)
    p.add_argument('--text', default=None)
    p.add_argument('-n', type=int, default=10)
    p.add_argument('--open', action='store_true')
    p.add_argument('--note', default='')
    p.add_argument('--days', default=None); p.add_argument('--day', default=None); p.add_argument('--today', action='store_true')
    p.add_argument('--force', action='store_true'); p.add_argument('--quiet', action='store_true'); p.add_argument('--all', action='store_true')
    p.add_argument('--phone', default=''); p.add_argument('--email', default=''); p.add_argument('--call', default='')
    p.add_argument('--why', default=''); p.add_argument('--at', default=None); p.add_argument('--every', default=None)
    a = p.parse_args()
    if a.cmd == 'status':
        status()
    elif a.cmd == 'config':
        print(json.dumps(store.load_config(), indent=2))
    elif a.cmd == 'set':
        try:
            patch = json.loads(a.arg or '')
        except Exception as e:
            sys.exit(f'set needs a JSON object: {e}')
        if 'phone_number' in patch or 'models' in patch:
            sys.exit('phone_number/models are changed by the admin (provisioning), not here.')
        apply(patch)
    elif a.cmd == 'set-followups':
        try:
            lst = json.loads(a.arg or '')
            assert isinstance(lst, list) and all(isinstance(x, str) for x in lst)
        except Exception:
            sys.exit('set-followups needs a JSON list of strings')
        cfg = store.load_config(); cfg['after_call']['follow_ups'] = lst
        store.save_config(cfg); print('Saved follow-ups.'); status()
    elif a.cmd == 'calls':
        db = store.db()
        q = 'SELECT * FROM calls' + (' WHERE handled_at IS NULL' if a.open else '') + ' ORDER BY started_at DESC LIMIT ?'
        rows = db.execute(q, (a.n,)).fetchall()
        if not rows:
            print('No calls yet.')
        for r in rows:
            print(f"{r['id']}  {local(r['started_at'])}  {r['duration_s']}s  from {fmt_phone(r['caller'])}  name={r['caller_name']}  status={r['status']}"
                  f"  {'HANDLED' if r['handled_at'] else 'open'}\n   message: {r['message']}\n   summary: {r['summary']}\n   callback: {fmt_phone(r['callback_number'])}"
                  f"  urgency: {r['urgency']}  intent: {r['intent']}\n   fields: {r['fields']}\n   appointment: {r['appointment']}  transfer: {r['transfer']}  spam: {r['spam']}  alerts: {r['alerts']}")
    elif a.cmd == 'call':
        r = store.db().execute('SELECT * FROM calls WHERE id=?', (a.arg,)).fetchone()
        if not r:
            sys.exit('No such call id. Use `phone calls`.')
        d = dict(r); tr = json.loads(d.pop('transcript') or '[]')
        d['started_at'] = local(d['started_at']); d['ended_at'] = local(d['ended_at'])
        d['caller'] = fmt_phone(d.get('caller'))
        d['callback_number'] = fmt_phone(d.get('callback_number'))
        print(json.dumps(d, indent=1))
        print('\nTranscript:')
        for x in tr:
            print(f"{x['role']}: {x['text']}")
    elif a.cmd == 'handled':
        db = store.db()
        n = db.execute('UPDATE calls SET handled_at=?, handled_note=? WHERE id=?', (store.iso(), a.note[:2000], a.arg)).rowcount
        print('Marked handled.' if n else 'No such call id.')
    elif a.cmd in ('on', 'off'):
        cfg = store.load_config(); cfg['enabled'] = a.cmd == 'on'; store.save_config(cfg)
        print(f"Phone agent is now {'ON: it answers calls again' if cfg['enabled'] else 'OFF: the AI drops incoming calls until you turn it back on'}."); status()
    elif a.cmd == 'emergency':
        pol = {'transfer': 'transfer', 'text': 'text', 'message': 'message'}.get(a.arg or '')
        if not pol:
            sys.exit('usage: phone emergency transfer|text|message')
        cfg = store.load_config(); cfg['emergency']['policy'] = pol
        cfg['options']['transfer'] = bool(pol == 'transfer' and (cfg['transfer'].get('targets')))
        errs = store.validate(cfg)
        if errs:
            sys.exit('Not saved: ' + '; '.join(errs))
        store.save_config(cfg); print('Saved. The next call uses it.'); status()
    elif a.cmd == 'booking':
        m = (a.arg or '').lower()
        if m not in ('live', 'request', 'off', 'link'):
            sys.exit('usage: phone booking live | request | off | link <https://booking-url>')
        cfg = store.load_config(); cfg['options']['appointments'] = m
        if m == 'link':
            if not (a.arg2 or '').startswith('http'):
                sys.exit('link mode needs the booking URL: phone booking link https://...')
            cfg['booking']['booking_link'] = a.arg2
        errs = store.validate(cfg)
        if errs:
            sys.exit('Not saved: ' + '; '.join(errs))
        store.save_config(cfg); print('Saved. The next call uses it.'); status()
    elif a.cmd == 'info':
        if not a.arg:
            print(store.load_config()['business_info']); return
        cfg = store.load_config(); cfg['business_info'] = a.arg
        errs = store.validate(cfg)
        if errs:
            sys.exit('Not saved: ' + '; '.join(errs))
        store.save_config(cfg); print('Saved (in the prompt on the next call).')
    elif a.cmd == 'faq':
        cfg = store.load_config(); fq = cfg.get('faq') or []
        if a.arg == 'list':
            for f in fq:
                print(f"Q: {f['q']}\nA: {f['a']}")
            return
        if a.arg == 'add' and a.arg2 and a.arg3:
            fq = [f for f in fq if f['q'] != a.arg2] + [{'q': a.arg2, 'a': a.arg3}]
        elif a.arg == 'rm' and a.arg2:
            fq = [f for f in fq if f['q'] != a.arg2]
        else:
            sys.exit('usage: phone faq add "Question" "Answer" | rm "Question" | list')
        cfg['faq'] = fq
        errs = store.validate(cfg)
        if errs:
            sys.exit('Not saved: ' + '; '.join(errs))
        store.save_config(cfg); print(f'Saved. {len(fq)} FAQ items.')
    elif a.cmd == 'kb':
        if a.arg == 'add':
            text = open(a.file).read() if a.file else a.text
            if not (a.arg2 and text):
                sys.exit('usage: phone kb add "Title" --file /path/doc.txt  (or --text "...")')
            print(f'Added "{a.arg2}": {store.kb_add(a.arg2, text)} searchable chunks.')
        elif a.arg == 'list':
            for d in store.kb_list():
                print(f"{d['title']}  ({d['chunks']} chunks, {d['chars']} chars, added {d['added_at']})")
            if not store.kb_list():
                print('Knowledge base is empty.')
        elif a.arg == 'rm' and a.arg2:
            print('Removed.' if store.kb_rm(a.arg2) else 'No such document.')
        elif a.arg == 'search' and a.arg2:
            for r in store.kb_search(a.arg2):
                print(f"[{r['title']}] {r['text'][:400]}\n")
        else:
            sys.exit('usage: phone kb add|list|rm|search')
    elif a.cmd == 'voices':
        cfg = store.load_config()
        print('GPT Live voices: ' + ', '.join(f"{v}{' (current)' if v == cfg['voice'] else ''}" for v in store.VOICES))
    elif a.cmd == 'voice':
        if a.arg not in store.VOICES:
            sys.exit('Not a GPT Live voice. Choose one of: ' + ', '.join(store.VOICES))
        cfg = store.load_config(); cfg['voice'] = a.arg; store.save_config(cfg); print(f'Voice is now {a.arg}; the next call uses it.')
    elif a.cmd == 'history':
        for e in store.history(15):
            print(f"#{e['id']} {local(e['ts'])} {e['kind']}{' (UNDONE)' if e.get('undone') else ''} {e.get('note') or ''}")
            for d in e['diff'][:8]:
                print('    ' + d)
    elif a.cmd == 'undo':
        r = store.undo()
        if not r:
            sys.exit('Nothing to undo.')
        print(f"Undid change #{r[0]['id']} ({local(r[0]['ts'])}). Now back to the previous setup:")
        for d in r[1][:12]:
            print('    ' + d)
    elif a.cmd == 'override':
        cfg = store.load_config(); ov = cfg.get('overrides') or []
        if a.arg == 'list':
            eff, act = store.effective_config(cfg)
            for o in ov:
                print(f"{o['id']}  {'ACTIVE' if o in act else 'inactive'}  from {local_iso(o.get('from'))} until {local_iso(o.get('until'))}  {json.dumps(o['set'])}  {o.get('note') or ''}")
            print('No overrides.' if not ov else '')
            return
        if a.arg == 'rm':
            ov = [o for o in ov if o['id'] != a.arg2]
        elif a.arg == 'add':
            try:
                patch = json.loads(a.arg2 or '')
                assert isinstance(patch, dict)
                import uuid
                o = {'id': 'ov-' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:6], 'set': patch, 'from': store.resolve_when(a.frm, cfg, 'from') if a.frm else None,
                     'until': store.resolve_when(a.until, cfg, 'until') if a.until else None, 'note': a.note or None, 'created': store.iso()}
            except Exception as e:
                sys.exit(f'override add needs a JSON patch and valid --from/--until: {e}')
            if o['from'] and o['until'] and o['until'] <= o['from']:
                sys.exit('--until must be after --from')
            ov = ov + [o]
        else:
            sys.exit('override add|list|rm')
        cfg['overrides'] = ov
        errs = store.validate(cfg)
        if errs:
            sys.exit('Not saved: ' + '; '.join(errs))
        # also validate each override applied on its own
        for o in ov:
            e2 = store.validate(store._merge({k: v for k, v in cfg.items() if k != 'overrides'}, o['set']))
            if e2:
                sys.exit('Not saved (override would make the setup invalid): ' + '; '.join(e2))
        store.save_config(cfg, note=f"override {a.arg} {a.arg2 or ''}"[:200]); print('Saved. Applies at call time and expires on its own.'); status()
    elif a.cmd == 'rule':
        cfg = store.load_config(); cr = cfg.setdefault('caller_rules', {'existing': {}, 'new': {}})
        if a.arg == 'clear' and a.arg2 in ('existing', 'new'):
            cr[a.arg2] = {}
        elif a.arg in ('existing', 'new') and a.arg2 == 'emergency' and a.arg3 in ('transfer', 'text', 'message'):
            cr[a.arg].setdefault('emergency', {})['policy'] = a.arg3
        elif a.arg in ('existing', 'new') and a.arg2 == 'booking' and a.arg3 in ('live', 'request', 'link', 'off'):
            cr[a.arg].setdefault('options', {})['appointments'] = a.arg3
        else:
            sys.exit('usage: phone rule existing|new emergency transfer|text|message | booking live|request|link|off | phone rule clear existing|new')
        errs = store.validate(cfg)
        if errs:
            sys.exit('Not saved: ' + '; '.join(errs))
        store.save_config(cfg, note=f'rule {a.arg} {a.arg2} {a.arg3 or ""}'); print('Saved.'); status()
    elif a.cmd == 'customers':
        cfg = store.load_config(); cu = cfg.get('customers') or []
        if a.arg == 'list':
            print('\n'.join(cu) or 'No extra customers (numbers that have called before also count as existing).'); return
        if a.arg == 'add' and a.arg2:
            cu = cu + [a.arg2] if a.arg2 not in cu else cu
        elif a.arg == 'rm' and a.arg2:
            cu = [x for x in cu if x != a.arg2]
        else:
            sys.exit('usage: phone customers add|rm <+E164> | list')
        cfg['customers'] = cu
        errs = store.validate(cfg)
        if errs:
            sys.exit('Not saved: ' + '; '.join(errs))
        store.save_config(cfg, note='customers'); print('Saved.')
    elif a.cmd in ('timing', 'cost'):
        import extras
        getattr(extras, a.cmd)(a, print)
    elif a.cmd in ('followup', 'contact'):
        import extras
        getattr(extras, a.cmd)(a, print)
    elif a.cmd == 'setup':
        import extras
        extras.setup(a, print)
    elif a.cmd in ('watch', 'review', 'briefing', 'proposal'):
        import extras
        getattr(extras, a.cmd)(a, print)
    elif a.cmd in ('standard', 'field', 'intent', 'closure', 'target', 'holiday', 'blackout'):
        edit(a)
    else:
        print(__doc__)


def edit(a):
    cfg = store.load_config()
    it = cfg['intake']; sub = a.arg
    if a.cmd == 'standard':
        k, onoff = a.arg, a.arg2
        if k not in it['standard'] or onoff not in ('on', 'off'):
            sys.exit('usage: phone standard <name|callback_number|email|reason> on|off [required|optional] [--ask "wording"]')
        it['standard'][k]['on'] = onoff == 'on'
        if a.arg3 in ('required', 'optional'):
            it['standard'][k]['required'] = a.arg3 == 'required'
        if a.ask:
            it['standard'][k]['ask'] = a.ask
    elif a.cmd == 'holiday':
        b = cfg['booking']; hl = b.setdefault('holidays', {}).setdefault('closed', [])
        if sub == 'list':
            import datetime as _dt
            y = _dt.date.today().year
            for k, nm in store.US_HOLIDAYS.items():
                d = store.us_holidays(y)[k]
                if d < _dt.date.today():
                    d = store.us_holidays(y + 1)[k]
                print(f"{k:12} {nm:28} next {d}  {'CLOSED (not bookable)' if k in hl else 'open (bookable)'}")
            return
        if a.arg2 not in store.US_HOLIDAYS or sub not in ('open', 'close'):
            sys.exit('usage: phone holiday list | open <key> | close <key>; keys: ' + ', '.join(store.US_HOLIDAYS))
        b['holidays']['closed'] = [k for k in hl if k != a.arg2] + ([a.arg2] if sub == 'close' else [])
    elif a.cmd == 'blackout':
        b = cfg['booking']; bl = b.get('blackout_dates') or []
        if sub == 'list':
            print(json.dumps(bl)); return
        if sub == 'add':
            spec = a.arg2 or ''
            e = {'start': spec.split('..')[0], 'end': spec.split('..')[1]} if '..' in spec else {'date': spec}
            if a.arg3:
                e['name'] = a.arg3
            bl = bl + [e]
        elif sub == 'rm':
            bl = [x for x in bl if (x if isinstance(x, str) else (x.get('date') or x.get('start'))) != a.arg2]
        else:
            sys.exit('blackout add|rm|list')
        b['blackout_dates'] = bl
    else:
        def js():
            try:
                v = json.loads(a.arg2 or '')
                assert isinstance(v, dict)
                return v
            except Exception:
                sys.exit(f'{a.cmd} {sub} needs a JSON object')
        if a.cmd == 'field':
            if sub == 'list':
                for c in it['custom']:
                    print(json.dumps(c))
                return
            if sub == 'add':
                v = js(); it['custom'] = [c for c in it['custom'] if c['key'] != v.get('key')] + [v]
            elif sub == 'rm':
                it['custom'] = [c for c in it['custom'] if c['key'] != a.arg2]
            else:
                sys.exit('field add|rm|list')
        elif a.cmd == 'intent':
            if sub == 'add':
                v = js(); it['intents'] = [c for c in it['intents'] if c['name'] != v.get('name')] + [v]
            elif sub == 'rm':
                it['intents'] = [c for c in it['intents'] if c['name'] != a.arg2]
                for c in it['custom']:
                    c['intents'] = [n for n in c.get('intents') or [] if n != a.arg2]
            else:
                sys.exit('intent add|rm')
        elif a.cmd == 'closure':
            cl = cfg.get('closures') or []
            if sub == 'add':
                cl = cl + [js()]
            elif sub == 'rm':
                cl = [c for c in cl if a.arg2 not in (c.get('date'), c.get('start'), c.get('name'))]
            else:
                sys.exit('closure add|rm')
            cfg['closures'] = cl
        elif a.cmd == 'target':
            t = cfg['transfer']; tg = t.get('targets') or []
            if sub == 'add':
                v = js(); tg = [x for x in tg if x['number'] != v.get('number')] + [v]
            elif sub == 'rm':
                tg = [x for x in tg if x['number'] != a.arg2]
            elif sub == 'clear':
                tg = []
            else:
                sys.exit('target add|rm|clear')
            t['targets'] = tg; t['number'] = tg[0]['number'] if tg else ''
    errs = store.validate(cfg)
    if errs:
        sys.exit('Not saved: ' + '; '.join(errs))
    store.save_config(cfg)
    print('Saved. The next call uses it.')
    status()


main()
